last week we heard from so many of you  about that big increase in your gas bill  so today the southwest gas corporation  began a five-day hearing about an  increase to their natural gas utility  service christian casares has been  looking into this matter which has a  whole lot of customers speaking out  again that's right brian denise well  southwest gas is proposing an annual  increase which is actually broken into  two parts now if approved northern  nevada would get a 3.81 percent increase  and southern nevada would be a 5.60  increase now the hearing for this  proposal began this morning and it  continues until friday i reached out to  the public utilities commission and they  told me they do not comment on ongoing  matters they say the approved increase  would impact the average monthly single  family residential bill for natural gas  service in southern nevada by 3.39 or  about 7.44  northern nevada customers can expect a  3.49  charge or about 4.55 percent boost in  their bill now according to the  company's website that increase would  provide a 28.7 million dollar increase  in revenue to cover the company's  current cost to provide safe and  reliable natural gas service here in  nevada now last week hundreds of emails  poured into our newsroom about an  increase in recent bills now in a  statement southwest gas said they  understand customers may be experiencing  natural gas bills which are higher than  expected which is likely due to natural  gas price increases between 2020 and  2021 as well as increased natural gas  usage during the winter months now i  also reached out to southwest gas today  about the proposed rate increase which  if approved would go into effect in  april as of now i'm still waiting for a  response christian gaston is live local  now
 

